.git
.gitignore
.github
.venv
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# runtime/ is BOTH the tradex_runtime workspace member and local broker/state
# data — the same split the root .gitignore documents. Excluding it wholesale
# would drop the package the Dockerfile copies and `uv sync --frozen` installs,
# so the state stays excluded (default deny, it holds the broker token and the
# instrument dumps) and only the package comes back.
runtime/
!runtime/pyproject.toml
!runtime/src/
# data/ is excluded by the build spec: history and instrument dumps are
# operator-supplied at run time, never baked into the image.
data/
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
**/*.db
graphify-out/
docs/superpowers/
